{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Joseph could no longer restrain himself.</b> The meaning is that he could not muster the strength to wait until all the attendants would leave of their own accord, and he cried out in a loud voice, ״הוֹצִיאוּ כָל אִישׁ״ — meaning, quickly; not that they should tell them to leave, for when they leave of their own accord they would leave slowly, and he could not bear the length of time the departure would take. And it says <b>and no one stood</b>, meaning, no man lingered, but quickly they went out immediately, all together." "<b>When Joseph made himself known.</b> The meaning is, for the sake of making himself known to his brothers — meaning, making the matter known so that they would recognize and acknowledge that he is Joseph, and this required him to bring them to recognition of him, and he did not wish to dishonor his brothers by having them be regarded as people capable of such wickedness as selling their brother. And it says immediately afterward: <b>And he gave forth his voice in weeping, and the Egyptians heard</b>, etc. — this tells us that what prevented those below from knowing when he made himself known to his brothers was not on his own account, for he cried aloud and the entire city heard the matter; rather, it was on account of his brothers' shame that he did what was mentioned."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:45.523183713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}